    <bpmn:process id="W_W5553" name="W5553. Mobile App Store Removal, Policy-Violation Response &amp; Re-Listing Recovery Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Apple App Store or Google Play rejects a pending release, removes/deactivates the live BuildRight app, or takes down listing metadata — App Review rejection, live-app removal for policy violation, or a developer-account action
Frequency: Release rejections: occasional, a few per year; live-app removal or developer-account action: rare, fewer than one event per several years
Volume: 1 event × the digital-engagement app population per the VS-75 canon × 2 storefronts (iOS App Store + Google Play per W2647); a live removal halts all new downloads and all update delivery to installed bases on the affected storefront
Owner: Digital Product Manager
Participants: IT (mobile engineering), Marketing (customer comms), CRM-Loyalty Manager (W2649 loyalty continuity), Customer Service Representative, CIO, CMO, VP Legal / DPO (privacy-policy findings per W2652)
Source: workflow W5553 — Mobile App Store Removal, Policy-Violation Response &amp; Re-Listing Recovery Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5553_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5553_Lane1" name="Digital Product Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5553_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5553_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5553_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5553_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5553_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5553_Lane2" name="IT">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5553_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5553_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5553_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5553_Start4" name="Apple App Store or Google Play rejects a pending release, removes/deactivates the live…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5553_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5553_Task5" name="Detection &amp; classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Detection &amp; classification: App Store Connect / Play Console notice or release-pipeline rejection; classify: (a) App Review rejection of a pending release, (b) live-app removal/deactivation, (c) metadata/listing takedown, (d) developer-account action; capture the cited guideline clause and the appeal path/deadline
Responsible (R): Digital Product Manager / IT
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: &lt; 4 h</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5553_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5553_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5553_Task6" name="Impact assessment &amp; customer comms">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Impact assessment &amp; customer comms: quantify the affected surface (downloads halted? updates halted? push still functional on installed bases?); publish interim-channel guidance — mobile-web store, hotline, social channels (W948 class) — via push (W2648) while the binary still runs, and through the loyalty desk (W2649 continuity)
Responsible (R): Digital Product Manager / Marketing / Customer Service Representative
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: &lt; 24 h</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5553_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5553_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5553_Task7" name="Root-cause fix by class">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Root-cause fix by class: (a) privacy/data-declaration finding → fix the privacy manifests and SDK data flows per the W2652 discipline, with the DPO verifying no local RA 10173 issue mirrors it; (b) payment-rule finding → remove or adjust the violating flow; (c) content/metadata finding → listing correction per W2647; (d) binary defect → engineering fix through the paved-road release rings (W5517 class)
Responsible (R): IT / Digital Product Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2–10 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5553_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5553_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5553_Task8" name="Appeal &amp; expedited review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Appeal &amp; expedited review: file the platform appeal with the remediation evidence (diff, policy analysis, corrected declarations); request expedited review where customer impact is live; track daily
Responsible (R): Digital Product Manager / IT
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Appeal window</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5553_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5553_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5553_Task9" name="Re-listing &amp; verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Re-listing &amp; verification: app/release restored; verify install, update and deep-link paths, push delivery, and loyalty sign-in across both storefronts; re-verify listing metadata per W2647; resume the release cadence
Responsible (R): IT / Digital Product Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5553_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5553_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5553_Task10" name="Prevention register">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Prevention register: add the violated clause to the release checklist (a store-policy gate in the W2647 listing discipline and the W5521-class release calendar); assign the quarterly platform-policy watch; log the event in the channel-risk register feeding the platform-dependency review
Responsible (R): Digital Product Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 4 h</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5553_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5553_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5553_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5553_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-454 (ensure controlled execution — Mobile App Product &amp; Feature Management (PA-75.1).) | - CTL-203 (protect mobile-app customer data &amp; release quality.) | - operational: no appeal is filed without the remediation evidence attached; the violated clause enters the release checklist before cadence resumes
Owner: Digital Product Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
